# Secrets — never cross the membrane
gate/data/.gate_token
gate/data/.gate_daemon
rhythm/.mail_creds
tools/dispatcher_bot/.env

# The body's rawest channel — Kevin's delete controls these; they never cross
rhythm/_pages_gated/
rhythm/pages_inbox/
rhythm/outbox/
rhythm/.last_brief

# Runtime / generated
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Staged-worktree scoping, 2026-08-11 (Kevin's mark, session 8a8f232e) ---
# This repo tracks ONLY the open game-development footprint: nesi/, counsel/,
# inbox/, the four ledger-tool scripts, and the three standing ledgers.
# Everything else at the DSS root (legal/financial/personal material, other
# project trees, tools/'s many unrelated subsystems) is ignored by default so
# a future `git add -A` here can never sweep it in.
/*
!/nesi/
!/counsel/
!/inbox/
!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/marks.py
!/tools/gates.py
!/tools/decisions.py
!/tools/surface.py
# The Group K scanner, 2026-08-27/28 (Kevin's mark, "build it" on
# PREFLIGHT_2026-08-27_k_lens.md). Reuses library_lens.js's own scoring
# discipline against the library-at-large rather than retired-build lineage.
# Tracked so the instrument travels with the corpus it scans.
!/tools/k_lens.js
# The boot hook, 2026-08-17 (Kevin's mark: "set up the hook layer"). It reads
# LEARNED.md and injects it at SessionStart, which is what makes the route a
# filesystem fact rather than an instruction. Tracked so it travels with the
# deposit it carries. The settings.json that calls it stays out by the rule
# above, so a clone gets the script and wires it by hand.
!/tools/boot_hook.py
# The harness boot layer, 2026-08-31 (Kevin's mark: "add them to the
# allowlist"). Same gap boot_hook.py's own entry above already named,
# never closed for its sibling: boot_hook_harness.py is wired into
# settings.json's SessionStart hook exactly the way boot_hook.py is, and
# calls the three instruments below with --summary on every boot, but none
# of the five files were tracked — a boot path that does not survive a
# checkout is not routed, and this one wasn't. Closed the same day
# agent_usage_check.js was built (skill/agent usage had no instrument for
# agents at all before this).
!/tools/boot_hook_harness.py
!/tools/check_harness.js
!/tools/framing_check_skills.js
!/tools/lens_usage_check.js
!/tools/agent_usage_check.js
# The counsel seats' definition files, 2026-08-13 (Kevin's mark, THE FULL CIRCLE).
# The trim tabs change how the five seats read and had no version history at all.
# Narrow on purpose: agents/ only — settings.json and settings.local.json stay out.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
# Widened 2026-08-19, Kevin's mark ("track .claude/skills in git too"). Four
# skills built and adversarially proven the same day (cold-walk,
# conservation-harness, threshold-sweep, the-closing-check — see
# game-craft.md's own dated section on them) had no version history either,
# same gap the line above already named for the agents. Still narrow:
# skills/ only, alongside agents/ — settings.json and settings.local.json
# stay out, unchanged from the original mark.
!/.claude/skills/
# The boot path, 2026-08-17 (Kevin's mark: "lift the freeze and route LEARNED.md
# into the boot path"). It is the only file in this repo that loads on its own,
# and the root's default-ignore would have made it vanish on clone — a boot path
# that does not survive a checkout is not routed. This line only; the vendor
# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md is outside the repo and stays suspended.
!/CLAUDE.md
# The retirement ledger, un-ignored 2026-08-17. The comment above names "the three
# standing ledgers" and this is the fourth, added later and never let through — so
# a clone got the marks, the gates and the offers, and lost every record of what
# had been retired. A retirement that does not travel is a thing that comes back.
!/RETIRED.jsonl
!/MARKS_LOG.jsonl
!/OPEN_GATES.jsonl
!/DECISIONS_OFFERED.jsonl
!/.gitignore

# The gate's own tool code, un-ignored 2026-08-26 (Kevin's mark: "carve out
# gate.py + tools only"). `gate.py apply` — the delta-ingestion command this
# session built — had no version history, same gap RETIRED.jsonl closed on
# 2026-08-17. Narrow on purpose: the backend script, its sibling script, its
# own nested .gitignore (protects data/.gate_token), and the README that
# documents them. gate_data.json, THE_GATE.html, state_view.html, and every
# other generated/felt-read file stay local and untracked, unchanged.
!/gate/
/gate/*
!/gate/gate.py
!/gate/update_state_view.py
!/gate/README.md
!/gate/.gitignore

# Within nesi/: exclude the already-independently-gitted 3D tree, binary
# exports, archival compost, and quarantine — none of these are "open
# development" in the staged sense.
/nesi/world3d/
/nesi/world2d/export/
/nesi/_compost/
/nesi/*.exe
/nesi/*.exe.bak*
/nesi/_intake_quarantine_2026-08-10/

# Ephemeral widget renders
/_widgets/

# Cold-walk artifacts are regenerated per run with a fresh store key (2026-08-12)
nesi/game2d/coldwalk/

# the runner's own night scratch (run copies, state, the morning walk)
nesi/game2d/.night/
